  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total obligations in Kansas are $2.7B for FY2026 to date. Award count in Kansas is 21,928 and average award size in Kansas is $124K. Obligations in Kansas fell 23.8% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buying agency in Kansas with obligations of $1.5B, followed by the Department of Defense with obligations of $541M and the Department of Transportation with obligations of $462M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor in Kansas with obligations of $1.3B, followed by INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. with obligations of $381M and ENVISION XPRESS INC with obligations of $93.6M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry in Kansas with obligations of $1.3B, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is the second industry with obligations of $380M. These totals are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Kansas trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations by fiscal year show that FY22 reached $4.2B and obligations then moved through FY23 at $3B, FY24 at $3.3B, and FY25 at $3.6B before falling to $2.7B in FY26. Year over year, obligations fell 23.8%. Award count in FY26 to date is 21,928 with average award size of $124K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate federal contracts in Kansas?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry with obligations of $1.3B, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing follows with obligations of $380M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor with obligations of $1.3B, and INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. is the second vendor with obligations of $381M."
      }
    ]
  },
